<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Hoceima</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alhucemas, Villa Sanjurjo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al Hoceima is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, in the Rif. It lies near the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekor">Nekor</a>, capital of an early Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>. The modern town was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> as Villa Sanjurjo after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhucemas-landing">Alhucemas landing</a> of 1925 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rif-war">Rif War</a> and returned to Morocco in 1956. In 2016–2017 it was the centre of the Hirak Rif protest movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-hoceima.jpg" alt="Al Hoceima" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdel Jalil Bouhaj · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al_Hoceima_Quemado.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
